# Reading: First Position in C (repertoire plan: st-read-first-c). An original 16-bar reading
# study in C major on strings 3, 2 and 1, from the open G (string 3) up to G on string 1, fret 3.
# Only quarter and half notes; no ties or dotted notes. Mostly steps (each note the next letter
# up or down), with some thirds as the small skips. Four phrases of four bars: the first ends on
# G (a half close), the second on C, the third climbs from string 3 to the top G in three short
# steps (A B C, D E F, E F G) and pauses on G7, the fourth begins like the first and closes on C.
# First position: finger 1 plays fret 1, finger 2 fret 2, finger 3 fret 3, on every string.
# The notes: G (3:0), A (3:2), B (2:0), C (2:1), D (2:3), E (1:0), F (1:1), G (1:3).
# The teacher strums C, Am, Dm, G and G7 underneath.
